  <!-- Privacy Policy Modal -->
  <div class="app-modal-overlay info-dialog-overlay" id="privacyModal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="privacyModalTitle" aria-describedby="privacyModalSummary">
    <div class="app-modal-box info-dialog">
      <div class="modal-head">
        <h3 class="modal-title" id="privacyModalTitle">Privacy Policy</h3>
        <button type="button" class="modal-close-btn" aria-label="Close" onclick="closeModal('privacyModal')">✕</button>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body info-dialog-body">
        <p class="info-dialog-intro" id="privacyModalSummary">This notice explains how the current PICKLERS installation uses information when you create an account, book a court, or join an open play session.</p>
        <section>
          <h4>Information used by the app</h4>
          <p>Your profile can include your name, email address, phone number, profile picture, and playing level. The app stores account and booking records, Pickle Credits transactions, notifications, favorites, and community posts or messages you submit. Passwords are stored as password hashes.</p>
          <p>Facility applicants also provide business details, a facility address, and verification documents for application review.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h4>Why it is used and who can see it</h4>
          <p>Information supports sign-in, account management, reservations, facility operations, wallet records, and support conversations. Relevant booking information is available to facility operators and authorized staff. Authorized administrators can review operational records and facility applications.</p>
          <p>Messages you send are visible to the participants in the conversation. Share only information you intend others to see.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h4>Location, browser storage, and external services</h4>
          <p>If you allow location access, the app uses your coordinates to estimate travel times and identify your area. Reverse-geocoding requests send coordinates to OpenStreetMap's Nominatim service. Facility coordinates supplied during an application are stored with that application.</p>
          <p>Browser storage remembers preferences such as your theme, and a session cookie keeps you signed in. Browser notifications depend on your permission. Pages also request typefaces from Google Fonts; external services receive the connection information needed to serve those requests.</p>
          <p>Displaying a booking pass requests a QR code from QR Server using the booking reference, facility name, and court name. Opening a directions link sends the destination to your chosen map service.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h4>Payments and account deletion</h4>
          <p>PICKLERS records the payment method selected for a booking and its Pickle Credits transactions. External payment arrangements are handled with the facility; this installation does not process real-money top-ups through a payment gateway.</p>
          <p>You can edit your profile in Settings. The available Delete Account action deactivates your account and replaces its sign-in email; it does not erase all stored records. Booking, financial, and other linked records remain. Account deletion follows the same cancellation rules for eligible active bookings and is restricted for administrator and facility owner accounts.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h4>Privacy questions and retention</h4>
          <p>Contact the person or organization running this installation to ask about access, corrections, deletion, or retained information. An operator privacy contact and a published retention schedule have not been configured for this installation.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
      <div class="info-dialog-footer">
        <button type="button" class="btn-view-courts info-dialog-close" onclick="closeModal('privacyModal')">Close</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Terms of Service Modal -->
  <div class="app-modal-overlay info-dialog-overlay" id="termsModal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="termsModalTitle" aria-describedby="termsModalSummary">
    <div class="app-modal-box info-dialog">
      <div class="modal-head">
        <h3 class="modal-title" id="termsModalTitle">Terms of Service</h3>
        <button type="button" class="modal-close-btn" aria-label="Close" onclick="closeModal('termsModal')">✕</button>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body info-dialog-body">
        <p class="info-dialog-intro" id="termsModalSummary">These terms describe account use, booking responsibilities, and the payment and cancellation rules implemented in this PICKLERS installation.</p>
        <section>
          <h4>Your account and conduct</h4>
          <p>Provide accurate account and booking information, keep your sign-in details private, and use only an account you are authorized to access. Treat players, facility staff, and other users respectfully. Do not send abusive content or interfere with another person's account or reservation.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h4>Booking requests and venue rules</h4>
          <p>Court reservations and Open Play requests are subject to facility owner approval and availability. Check the status in My Bookings before travelling; submitting a request does not guarantee a confirmed reservation or seat.</p>
          <p>Review the facility, date, time, price, and payment method before submitting. Arrive on time, follow the host venue's safety and equipment rules, and respect court etiquette.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h4>Payments</h4>
          <p>Pickle Credits bookings use your available wallet balance. Real-money top-ups are currently unavailable. Selecting an external payment method does not confirm payment: GCash, Maya, and cash arrangements must be made directly with the facility.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h4>Cancellations and Pickle Credits refunds</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Pending Pickle Credits bookings:</strong> you may withdraw an unapproved request for a full refund of the amount charged, including requests made within 24 hours of play.</li>
            <li><strong>Confirmed Pickle Credits bookings:</strong> a full refund applies only when cancelled at least 24 hours before the scheduled start. If cancelled within 24 hours, no refund applies.</li>
            <li><strong>After the start:</strong> Confirmed bookings cannot be cancelled after play starts. Pending requests may still be withdrawn.</li>
            <li><strong>Open Play:</strong> the same pending and confirmed rules apply to your booked session date, including a selected occurrence of an everyday session.</li>
            <li><strong>Free sessions:</strong> there is nothing to refund when no Pickle Credits were charged.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>External payments are not refunded in-app; contact the facility about any payment or refund arranged outside PICKLERS. The cancellation dialog shows the applicable information before you confirm.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h4>Account closure and assistance</h4>
          <p>Account deletion does not erase booking or financial history or change the cancellation policy. For a venue issue, contact the facility. For an account or technical issue, contact the installation operator using the guidance in Help &amp; Support.</p>
          <p class="info-dialog-note">Closing this dialog only returns you to Settings; it does not record a new agreement or change a booking.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
      <div class="info-dialog-footer">
        <button type="button" class="btn-view-courts info-dialog-close" onclick="closeModal('termsModal')">Close</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

